WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.566
Choose storage by describing the application’s
operations before choosing a product Record the
shape

00:00:06.566 --> 00:00:12.739
and size of the data, lookup keys, range queries,
joins, update rates and required guarantees.

00:00:12.739 --> 00:00:12.936
No.

00:00:12.936 --> 00:00:19.502
Large-object delivery and concurrent invariant-
preserving updates have different access patterns
and

00:00:19.502 --> 00:00:21.406
can justify different stores.

00:00:21.406 --> 00:00:27.619
A checkout updates several related facts: the order,
its line items and the remaining gift-card

00:00:27.619 --> 00:00:32.589
balance Atomicity means these changes commit
together or roll back together.

00:00:32.589 --> 00:00:32.785
No.

00:00:32.785 --> 00:00:39.063
The operation needs appropriate isolation, locking
or an atomic conditional update, plus balance

00:00:39.063 --> 00:00:41.155
validation and failure handling.

00:00:41.155 --> 00:00:47.446
Operational transaction processing usually consists
of many small reads and writes, such as fetching

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:53.674
a student’s enrolments or reserving a seat Analytics
may scan years of records to compare enrolment

00:00:53.674 --> 00:00:54.114
trends.

00:00:54.114 --> 00:01:00.342
The calculation needs only selected attributes, so
reading and compressing those columns can reduce

00:01:00.342 --> 00:01:01.474
I/O substantially.
